Q. What is Object-Oriented Programming (OOP)?

Answer:

Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) is a programming paradigm that organizes code into objects. Objects contain attributes (data) and methods (functions). OOP helps write code that is modular, reusable, maintainable, and easy to manage, especially in large projects.

Quick Revision

Python me everything is an object.
Object Class se banta hai.
Class = Blueprint (Design).
Object = Blueprint se bani actual cheez.
Object ke Attributes (data) aur Methods (functions) hote hain.
. (dot operator) se methods aur attributes access karte hain.
OOP (Object-Oriented Programming) ek programming paradigm hai jo code ko objects me organize karta hai.
OOP ka use bade projects (jaise Amazon, Netflix, etc.) me code ko clean, reusable aur maintainable banane ke liye kiya jata hai.




