Q1. What is __init__()?

__init__() is a special constructor method that is automatically called when an object is created. It is used to initialize object attributes.

Q2. What is self?

self is a reference to the current object (instance) of the class. It allows us to access the object's attributes and methods.

Q3. Why do we write self.name = name?

Because the parameter name is temporary, while self.name stores the value permanently inside the object.

