3. Class Object Attribute (Static Attribute)

Class ke andar aur __init__() ke bahar jo variable banta hai, use Class Object Attribute kehte hain.

Example
class PlayerCharacter:

    membership = True

    def __init__(self, name, age):
        self.name = name
        self.age = age

Yahan:

membership = True

ek Class Object Attribute hai.

Features
Sabhi objects ke liye same hota hai.
Static value hoti hai.
Memory me sirf ek baar store hota hai.
Har object ise share karta hai.

Access
print(PlayerCharacter.membership)
print(player1.membership)
print(player2.membership)

Output:

True
True
True


4. Instance Attribute (Object Attribute)

Jo variables __init__() ke andar self ke saath bante hain, unhe Instance Attributes kehte hain.

Example
class PlayerCharacter:

    def __init__(self, name, age):
        self.name = name
        self.age = age

Features
Har object ke liye alag value hoti hai.
Dynamic hote hain.
Object create hone par bante hain.

Example
player1 = PlayerCharacter("Cindy", 44)
player2 = PlayerCharacter("Tom", 21)

Output:

player1.name → Cindy
player2.name → Tom




