Q1. What is MRO?

Answer:

MRO (Method Resolution Order) is the order in which Python searches for methods and attributes in an inheritance hierarchy.

Q2. Why is MRO needed?

Because in Multiple Inheritance, more than one parent class may contain the same method or attribute. MRO decides which one Python should use.

Q3. How can we check MRO?
ClassName.mro()

or

ClassName.__mro__
Q4. What algorithm does Python use for MRO?

Answer:

Python uses the C3 Linearization Algorithm to determine the Method Resolution Order.

🔥 Quick Revision
MRO (Method Resolution Order) = Python ka search order for methods and attributes.
MRO mainly Multiple Inheritance me important hota hai.
Python conflicts ko MRO ke according resolve karta hai.
MRO check karne ke liye ClassName.mro() ya ClassName.__mro__ use karte hain.
Har class ka last parent object hota hai.
Bahut complex inheritance code ko difficult bana deta hai, isliye Multiple Inheritance ka use carefully karna chahiye.